{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790513030,"nonce":"zatBlRtQEgfWrCIhI77OsGAWSo8=","message":"Done in caribou acee077 with ash bea61ac. A plugin crate declared with link = \"side\" is built by 'cargo rustc --crate-type staticlib -Z build-std=std,panic_abort' with -Crelocation-model=pic -Ctarget-feature=+mutable-globals and caribou_abi's side_module feature. It is then linked by rust-lld as a --experimental-pic -shared side module that exports its members' link symbols, written beside the program as \u003cplugin\u003e.wasm. Under side_module, the plugin allocates through the program's malloc and fetches the host table on first use through the import caribou_host_table, which caribou-runtime exports, so nothing has to call its entry. Ash's HostLink.library makes each linked call go through a slot that emit_late_init fills with hlp_aot_symbol(lib, symbol). tests/linked.rs runs the math plugin both linked and as a side module, with the same results. A libm import (hypot) is answered by the runtime object since wren_lift 2bd8f3f. Limits, from Ash: the browser host refuses dlopen (ash aca00a1), and threaded wasm programs can't load side modules (ash c639f0d). Plugin instances and Value/Buffer/Enum casts in either mode are 9203778.","files":null}]}